{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Gad, a troop shall troop upon him.</b> Many troops shall come against him for war, and at the start of the battle he shall strike them a great blow, as it is written (Deuteronomy 33:20) ״וְטָרַף זְרוֹעַ אַף קָדְקֹד״ — for it is hide for hide, and when one strikes with the sword, the one struck raises his hand to shield his head; therefore the hero first tears the arm and cuts it in two until the sword passes through to the skull. But Jacob speaks of the end of the battle, when his enemies turn their backs and flee — and the heel of the pursued is close to the pursuer, all the more so when he falls and stumbles in his fall, and then he shall cut off and sever his heels. This is what it says ״וְהוּא יָגֻד עָקֵב״, for ״יָגֻד״ means cutting off, from the language of ״גּוֹדּוּ אִילָנָא״."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:34:28.198560003Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}